      "text": "This is sort of a rhetorical question. God who created the heavens and the earth and everything in them. Of course, He knows what, you know, what, everything that He created. He's fully aware of all the creation that He made. I mean, in the Quran, there is even a verse that says \"not a single leaf falls without Him being knowing all that.\" So, if we know, if we can count, if it is possible to count how many trees are there in the world and if it is possible to count how many leaves in every tree, which is impossible for any human being, but God knows every single leaf that falls. That is how far, we cannot imagine how great is God. So, we cannot even hide anything from God. You know, the children are usually very very, still very innocent. And they used to be, you know, talk to them about, you know, God and... The best way would be, in my experience, they can lie to you, but we told them that you cannot lie to God. You can lie to your parents, you can lie, but God will always know. So, in the end, they are the ones who keep saying this all the time. God always knows whether we declare anything or we keep it secret.",
